cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the evidence package, please cite it as below."
title: "TRACE-C: rank-calibrated relational anomaly detection for multi-stream operational telemetry"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Faucher
    given-names: Matthew
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0005-5238-731X
version: 0.1.0
date-released: '2026-08-19'
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Strictly-prior rank-calibrated anomaly detection over aligned multi-stream
  telemetry, with an evidence-bound reporting chain: rolling robust-z
  marginals, local/dependence/temporal channels, Fisher rank aggregation,
  disclosed selection rules with exchangeable-null reference counts, a frozen
  blind 2020 hold-out on public GB grid data, and committed machine-readable
  reports that bind the paper's tables and figures.
keywords:
  - anomaly detection
  - conformal prediction
  - multivariate time series
  - calibration
  - reproducibility
url: "https://github.com/mars-arch/trace-c"
repository-code: "https://github.com/mars-arch/trace-c"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.57967/hf/10063
    description: Hugging Face dataset DOI for the NESO evidence package
